"""Root self-service command runner (home side of cloudflare/control-plane/src/self-service.ts).

Polls GET /v1/machines/<id>/commands with the machine credential murage-control uses for the lease and heartbeat,
runs each command at most once, and reports it: POST commands/ack, or POST logs (collect_logs) / export-ready
(export_archive), which acknowledge the command themselves.

  restart_service    restart murage-home.service (normal mode)
  safe_mode          restart it with bots, schedules and add-ons paused, until the next start (/run/murage-safe-mode)
  update_software    fetch the signed release named by /etc/murage-home/release.json, verify, swap /opt/murage, restart;
                     /data (files, settings, logins) is not touched; every step is journaled (update-journal.json) and
                     committed only once the app answers its health check; otherwise, or after an interruption, the
                     previous release is put back
  reset_from_backup  with the home and its turn/browser slices confirmed stopped, keep the current /data as a complete
                     restic snapshot (exit 0 only; its exact id verified and recorded, kept keepSnapshotDays from
                     completion), then rebuild /data from the newest nightly confirmed complete; engine sign-ins and the
                     home's own sign-in state (devices, revocations, pair-hold ledger) stay current; the swap is recorded
                     durably outside the staging tree, so an interruption is undone exactly or finished
  undo_reset         put back exactly the snapshot that reset recorded
  collect_logs       recent journal lines of the allow-listed Murage units; only allowed diagnostic events (the shared
                     contract's logEvents) are sent, any other line becomes a count; scrubbed here and again by the
                     control plane; engine sign-in directories are never read
  export_archive     tar of /data without credentials, zstd, age-encrypted to a one-time key (given to age-keygen on
                     stdin, never written), at most maxBytes and never below the data disk's headroom, both enforced while
                     it is produced; uploaded to the backup space at the contract path; the key is sent once with
                     export-ready and never stored

Reboot is not here: the control plane power-cycles through the provider. Every command id is journaled in
/var/lib/murage-home/commands before it runs; a journaled command is never run again (an interrupted one is reported
failed, or done when an interrupted reset had already swapped the data in; at start the runner recovers interrupted
resets and undos whether or not the control plane still lists them). A command's expiresAt is its run deadline: it is
never started after it, and no irreversible step (a data swap, a code swap, an upload) begins after it, so the control
plane can fail the job once the deadline (plus a grace) passes. A finished result the control plane has not acknowledged is
re-sent on every loop, whether or not the command is still listed. Unknown kinds or payload fields are answered
"unsupported". No field ever reaches a shell: every process gets an argument vector. The wire shapes are pinned by
shared/self-service-contract.json.
"""
